      "Language": "ger",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We report about a 44-year-old woman who presented at our Orthopaedic Department suffering from persisting pain and a tumor of the right knee after open articulosynovectomy. MRI did not clarify the entity at all. The X-ray examination could identify an inlying compress after a synovectomy in 1999. The intra-articular foreign body could be removed by open revision surgery."},
